id: pm-rust-query-cost
title: Explain native list query work before materializing context
description: "Expose a bounded native read plan using existing projection behavior, without a JavaScript runtime dependency."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: native,performance,query-plan
created_at: "2026-10-25T23:54:19.370Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-30T20:12:22.316Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-30T20:12:21.441Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-26T02:32:56.000Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Estimates are explicitly bounded or unknown, never fictional exact costs.; A narrow projection plans less materialization than full bodies on a 10000-item fixture.; Explain performs zero mutations and works in a non-git tracker.; Typed SDK and CLI, compact TOON and JSON, typed remedies, docs and public tracker measurements; unchanged npm and Bun CI release gates pass."
parent: pm-rust-u4al
resolution: "Delivered by PR #117 (7b1fb7a): Explain native list work before requesting large context"
expected_result: "Estimates are explicitly bounded or unknown, never fictional exact costs.; A narrow projection plans less materialization than full bodies on a 10000-item fixture.; Explain performs zero mutations and works in a non-git tracker.; Typed SDK and CLI, compact TOON and JSON, typed remedies, docs and public tracker measurements; unchanged npm and Bun CI release gates pass."
actual_result: "PR #117 merged at 2026-10-26T02:32:56Z as 7b1fb7a; required CI passed on the merged head."
comments[11]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-25T23:54:46.624Z",codex-agent,"Overlap audit: current CLI 2026.10.25 exposes context intents, output receipts and vector query plans, not a native file-reader cost plan. pm-context (1dae20d) packs evidence; pm-rlm (62ed36e) budgets orchestration calls; pm-memory (5bd356e) stores guidance. Native read sessions bound delivery and memory. This feature explains native list projection and candidate work before execution. Core TypeScript contracts remain the semantic oracle, not a runtime dependency. Scope: read-only list brief/full planning; no import/export/sync, journals, lifecycle classification or shared mutable coordination added."
  "2026-10-26T00:00:28.960Z",codex-agent,"Design: strict typed brief/full list admission, streaming directory/byte ceilings, shared execution projector, conditional decoder-input and candidate bounds, explicit unknown wire/heap/time costs. No item decoding or status-role decisions during planning, no state writes, no new import/export/sync or coordination paths. Tests add 10000-item materialization comparison, 500 seeded replay sequences with SDK state read-back, and no-Git/no-Node CLI byte-preservation checks."
  "2026-10-26T00:06:30.861Z",codex-agent,"Public-data validation: archived only the public tracker at unbraind/pm-rust commit dc8d894d5d6feb597a33872aaed87a6249afadac into a non-git scratch directory, made 180 source files read-only, and removed Git/Node from runtime PATH. Both plans observed 87 candidates and 874647 source bytes. Brief decoder input: 23042 bytes; full: 874647 bytes. Compact JSON: 778/741 bytes. All source filenames and bytes unchanged; SHA256 e31f3451c807182d3edf06b5cfd61c7e2b421e49b7f9228f6f1b037915e89eb9. Debug-build planning medians over three runs were 36.19/17.94 ms, descriptive only: full planning bypasses projection work, so these are not execution speed estimates."
  "2026-10-26T00:08:10.721Z",codex-agent,"Pinned pm test --run --progress passed all three linked commands: query-cost unit 5/5 (including 500 seeded numeric/payload fuzz cases), SDK/CLI acceptance 2/2 (including 500 seeded operation sequences with older-input replays and randomized custom registries), shared projector 3/3. The 10000-item fixture measured 16598890 source bytes, 1518890 brief decoder bytes and 16598890 full decoder bytes. Local all-target clippy/typecheck passed. Automatic test-result persistence is disabled by project policy, so these outcomes are recorded here rather than claiming a stored test-run receipt."
  "2026-10-26T00:10:06.613Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: changed only the new scan accounting to charge complete source text instead of the shared projected decoder input. The 10000-item regression failed at its materialization-ratio assertion (0 passed, 1 failed), then production source was restored byte-for-byte. Restored targeted suites pass. Review also clarified item-file I/O separately from unknown auxiliary settings/registry I/O; the protocol now exposes item_read_bytes and auxiliary_read_bytes=null rather than implying a complete query-I/O upper bound."
  "2026-10-26T00:11:14.739Z",codex-agent,"Final local rerun after item/auxiliary I/O clarification: all 10 focused tests pass, including 500 model sequences and 500 extreme-admission cases; all-target clippy/typecheck and strict rustdoc pass. Public scratch validation repeated with the final protocol: 87 candidates, 874647 item source bytes, brief/full decoder input 23042/874647 bytes, JSON 832/795 bytes; all 180 public files retained the same digest. Added a Windows junction fixture alongside Unix symlinks so skipped foreign sources are verified across platforms. CI aggregate gates will supply full-suite and unchanged coverage evidence."
  "2026-10-26T00:12:27.779Z",codex-agent,"Changelog regeneration and verification passed without changing the generated file. Local strict tracker health reports pre-existing extension-host version skew and merge configuration drift, plus advisory guidance/provenance findings. No merge configuration or append-only history was repaired (outside this task). The clean CI checkout health gate will distinguish these environment findings from branch defects. No dependency pins or coverage thresholds changed."
  "2026-10-26T00:34:25.865Z",codex-agent,"CI run 40248325986: full functional suites passed on Ubuntu 655, macOS 642 and Windows 635 tests (zero failed/ignored). Bun release aggregate reached 100% lines/functions/branches but 24733/24739 regions: six missing error-propagation regions in new scanner I/O and CLI output. Adding deterministic real-I/O failure cases and removing an unnecessary fallible serialization boundary, without lowering thresholds. macOS context latency separately measured 258.8 ms against 250 ms; no threshold changed. PR 117 is temporarily draft until acceptance gates pass."
  "2026-10-26T00:40:54.273Z",codex-agent,"Coverage follow-up implemented using fallible I/O boundaries, without SDK mocks: real directory/metadata/open failures and a real write-only file handle read failure now prove refusal propagation; CLI dispatch proves broken writes/flushes propagate. Removed fallible serialization of an entirely infallible typed plan. Pinned pm test --run --progress passed all four linked commands: 6 query-cost, 2 SDK/CLI, 3 projector, 1 broken-output test (12 total). All-target clippy/typecheck, rustdoc and formatting passed. Both materialization and swallowed-iteration behavioral reverts produced expected assertion failures, then source was restored byte-for-byte and all 12 tests rerun successfully. Repeated public read-only validation retains 87 candidates, 874647 item bytes, brief/full decoder input 23042/874647 and JSON 832/795, with all 180 filenames/bytes unchanged."
  "2026-10-26T01:05:57.942Z",codex-agent,"Corrected-head CI 40250604530 passed all platform functional suites (657 Ubuntu, 644 macOS, 637 Windows), CodeQL and every latency job; fresh macOS context p95 was 139.45 ms against 250 ms. npm aggregate passed 1314 Rust tests across both passes, with 100% lines/functions/branches; one region remains at executable output-error propagation. The SDK scanner now has complete coverage. Added actual CLI closed-pipe checks for JSON and TOON so the shipped binary, as well as in-process dispatch, proves disconnected-consumer refusal. Thresholds remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-26T01:09:21.721Z",codex-agent,"Implementation and local verification complete: all four pinned linked-test commands passed again (6 + 2 + 3 + 1 = 12 tests), including production CLI closed-pipe refusals in JSON and TOON; Clippy/typecheck passed. The 17-entry history verified and the original branch history remained a byte-identical prefix. Supplemental flat-source overlap check of pm-rl found orchestration decision-query budgets, not a native item-file projection cost plan. PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/pull/117 . Final npm/Bun counts, coverage and clean-checkout health receipts will be published in that PR body and its checks at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/pull/117/checks . Releasing the implementation claim before the final verification run so CI checks the delivered tracking state too; item stays in progress for owner verification and closure."
